'' A '.rc' THAT INCLUDES <windows.h> BUILDS WITHOUT A WINDOWS SDK. llvm-rc finds that
'' header only in an SDK, so with none installed the line failed 'file not found'
'' (a user report). tiko now preprocesses with the bundled inc/win/rc headers as an
'' '-idirafter' fallback: an SDK, where there is one, still wins.
''
'' This machine's result does not show which header set was used -- with an SDK
'' installed, the SDK's. What it pins is the rest of the new path: LANG_ENGLISH and
'' winres.h resolve, the RCDATA file beside the '.rc' is still found from another
'' current directory and from the preprocessed copy's (the '.rc' is in src/, the copy
'' beside the exe), and the intermediate is deleted.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.rc-headers
'' CLEAN: build/.rc-headers/src
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/rc-headers.rc => build/.rc-headers/src/r.rc
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/rc-headers.bin => build/.rc-headers/src/rc-headers.bin
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/res.bas => build/.rc-headers/r.bas
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 build/.rc-headers/r.bas build/.rc-headers/src/r.rc -o build/.rc-headers/r.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: build/.rc-headers/r.exe
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.rc-headers/r.exe.rc1.res
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.rc-headers/r.exe.rc1.res.i
